<section class="landscape-hero" aria-labelledby="seasons-title">
  <div class="landscape-hero-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Landscape Deep Dive</p>
    <h1 id="seasons-title">Mukundara through the year</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The same hills look like three different places across a year: baked and leafless in May, deep green in
      August, gold and open in December. Water decides almost everything. This guide follows the habitat month by
      month, so you know what is changing and why.
    </p>
    <dl class="landscape-hero-facts" aria-label="Climate facts">
      <div><dt>Average rainfall</dt><dd>About 730 mm a year, over 90% between June and September</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Rainy days</dt><dd>About 27 in an average year, with large year-to-year variation</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Hottest</dt><dd>May and early June, up to about 46 °C</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Coldest</dt><dd>January, with night minimums near 8 °C</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="source-note">Climate figures: <a href="/resources/documents/mhtr-tiger-conservation-plan-bhainsrodgarh-core-addition/">Tiger Conservation Plan</a>, sections 2.1.6–2.1.7.</p>
  </div>
